y gifts  for them over here they're belts with a  nice chest belt buckle on them um and  we'll ask the players to come up they'll  pick one of their gifts and they'll get  their pairing number from there at the  very end i'll announce all the pairings  for round one which begins tomorrow at  one o'clock at the chess club if you  can't attend in person always remember  you can follow us on uschestjams.com  our amazing commentary team this year  i'm so excited we have grand masters  yasser sarawan christian carrillo and  none other than maurice ashley calling  all the play-by-play action if you  haven't heard them do commentary on  chess tune in for 10 minutes just watch  some of it i swear you'll be a convert  you'll love chess after that  i'm also very thankful to have an  amazing arbiting team here with us  you know you saw carol joracki earlier  who unfortunately passed away  during the pandemic  carol was kind of my guiding light when  it came to being an arbiter i remember  in 2009 when she came to st louis and  she was the chief arbor of the us and  u.s women's championship chris byrd was  one of the deputy arbiters and i i was  the other one and carol would sit down  with us and she was no nonsense i  remember her  she had a feed a handbook you know it's  this little booklet something like this  and she opened the page she had it like  memorized she opened the page and she  said tony this is how you do chess norms  i want you to sit down and calculate  every norm that could happen in the  tournament by hand i want you to figure  out if anybody is going to get an  international master norm or a grand  master norm and i tell you i have never  sweat so much for any test in my entire  life  carol will truly be missed but our  arbiting team that we have here  are more than capable of carrying that  that mantle and doing a wonderful job  our chief arbiter for the u.s  championship i'm sorry as i call you  guys if you would come up and help me  with the drawing of lo